9.3 Content Strategy: The "Anti-Social" Vibe
To maintain the "utility-first" vibe requested:

Zero "Feed" Algorithms: No algorithmic timelines or trending topics. Content is retrieved via active search or dashboard widgets only.

Curated Contributions: User-submitted content (like waveforms or field fixes) must pass a rigorous "Technical Review" (similar to code review) before publication, ensuring "Reference Grade" quality rather than forum hearsay.

Professional Tone: All system text, prompts, and tutorials should use standard automotive terminology (SAE J1930) to reinforce professional standards.


